<title>USA: Abbey National sets $500 mln perpetual notes.</title>
<headline>Abbey National sets $500 mln perpetual notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Abbey National Plc was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>The issue was increased in size by $200 million to meet investor demand, a Salomon source said.</p>
<p>BORROWER ABBEY NATIONAL PLC</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	   COUPON 7.35 PCT   MATURITY PERPETUAL</p>
<p>TYPE SUB RESET NOTES ISS PRICE 99.946  PAY FREQ N/A LAST MOODY AA3	 YIELD 7.358 PCT   FIRST PAY DATE N/A</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS				CALLABLE AFTER 10 YEARS</p>
<p>NOTES CALLABLE EVERY FIVE YEARS ON RESET</p>
<p>--U.S. corporate bond unit, 212-859-1672</p>
</text>
